# The Ruby sources, which is where most of the strings the app renders
# live. The three data files below carry translatable strings too — the
# desktop entry's Name/Comment/Keywords, every GSettings key's summary and
# description, and the AppStream metainfo's summary and description — and
# `rake pot` extracts them as well, through po/extract_data_strings.rb
# rather than rxgettext: rxgettext only understands Ruby, and xgettext
# itself needs a different frontend per format for these (intltool-extract,
# itstool), neither of which ships as a Ruby-reachable gem here.
data/com.github.huluti.Curtail.Rb.desktop
data/com.github.huluti.Curtail.Rb.gschema.xml
data/com.github.huluti.Curtail.Rb.metainfo.xml
lib/curtail_rb/compressor.rb
lib/curtail_rb/preferences_dialog.rb
lib/curtail_rb/result_item_manager.rb
lib/curtail_rb/result_item_row.rb
lib/curtail_rb/shortcuts_dialog.rb
lib/curtail_rb/tools.rb
lib/curtail_rb/window.rb
